# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Where a Windows release is collected on the way through this machine: an
# installer and the 138 MB core tarball. `dist/` was ignored and this was not,
# so 148 MB of build output sat in `git status` waiting to be added by accident.
dist-win/

# Tauri
desktop/src-tauri/target/
desktop/src-tauri/gen/
# The agent sidecar is a build artefact: scripts/sidecar.sh rebuilds it, and a
# 7 MB binary per platform has no business in the history.
desktop/src-tauri/binaries/

# Chromium fork — never commit the upstream tree, only patches
core/src/
core/depot_tools/
core/out/
core/.gclient*
# depot_tools bookkeeping. 154 files and 7.5 MB of a 10 MB repository, all of it
# regenerated by fetch.sh, none of it authored here.
core/.cipd/
core/.gcs_entries
core/dist/

# Secrets & local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
secrets/

# Build artifacts
*.dmg
*.msi
*.exe
*.app
*.zip

# Run logs. collector.log was committed in the initial scaffold and carried an
# absolute home directory into the history — the only /Users/ string in the whole
# tracked tree. It is a run log, not source.
*.log

# Python bytecode. examples/fury.py is the automation sample and importing it
# once leaves a .pyc beside it — which CPython stamps with the ABSOLUTE PATH of
# the source it was compiled from. One got committed, and it was the only thing
# in 1984 blobs of history that carried a real home directory:
#
#     /Users/<name>/Vibecoding/projects/antik/examples/fury.py
#
# Found by sweeping every blob that ever existed rather than the working tree,
# which is the only sweep that would have found it — the file was added once and
# never touched again. Removed from the history before the repository was
# published, because that is the last moment it is free to do.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local data
data/
tmp/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*

# Icons are generated from assets/icon.png by assets/generate.sh. The sources
# are committed; the derived sizes are not, so that nobody edits one of them
# separately and ships an app with two different logos.
core/branding/
